"example_id","slice","workflow_scope","example","business_payoff","step_1_terminal_check","step_2_action_or_pause","step_3_verification","closest_existing_software","terminal_and_method_source_urls","software_source_urls","assumptions"
1,1,"Cross-system business workflow","Hearthspan Fuel","$900 gross margin on a 100-tonne delivery","A weekly fuel tender names a specific ICE gasoil delivery month. The Terminal‚Äôs Futures Contract Table (CT <GO>) identifies the contract. Its official settlement of $690/t sets the customer price at $708/t under the agreed formula. A rolling front-month quote can refer to a different contract.","Match two 50-tonne supplier holds averaging $699/t landed. Draft the quote in the ERP. Pause if either hold expires before the customer‚Äôs bid deadline or the settlement is provisional.","Dispatcher confirms both holds and the owner approves the quote. Delivery receipts, a $70,800 paid invoice, and $69,900 in supplier bills verify the margin.","Agiblocks handles commodity contract pricing and invoicing.","https://assets.bbhub.io/professional/sites/10/Proprietary-Commodity-Data-on-Bloomberg-Brochure.pdf | https://assets.bbhub.io/professional/sites/10/Bloomberg-US-Treasury-Future-Tracker-Indices-Methodology.pdf | https://www.ice.com/products/34361119/Low-Sulphur-Gasoil-Futures/specs","https://www.agiboo.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/Agiblocks-Productsheet-V1.pdf","Fictional business and synthetic amounts. The scenario assumes authorized Terminal access, applicable data usage rights, and access to the listed destination systems. Some BFIX and FBAK uses require additional licensing, and BVAL requires applicable access."
2,1,"Cross-system business workflow","Switchyard Components","$450 incremental margin on a rush replacement","A supplier misses a delivery. Supply Chain Analysis (SPLC <GO>) links both backup distributors to the same upstream manufacturer. Verify whether they share a source before quoting either.","Match the part in the ERP and look for stock from another approved manufacturer in supplier portals. Draft a $650 rush charge against $200 incremental freight. Pause if the lot‚Äôs manufacturer is unconfirmed.","Buyer verifies the lot certificate and approves the quote. Proof of delivery, the paid rush charge, and the freight bill verify the $450.","Interos maps sub-tier suppliers and supports alternative sourcing.","https://professional.content.cirrus.bloomberg.com/professional2023/insights/markets/trade-war-and-tariffs-anatomy-of-winners-and-losers/","https://www.interos.ai/solutions/procurement-risk","Fictional business and synthetic amounts. The scenario assumes authorized Terminal access, applicable data usage rights, and access to the listed destination systems. Some BFIX and FBAK uses require additional licensing, and BVAL requires applicable access."
3,1,"Cross-system business workflow","Tern Guarantee Brokers","$1,200 replacement placement fee","A weekly guarantee review finds the issuing bank‚Äôs Fitch issuer rating fell to BBB+ in Credit Rating Profile (CRPR <GO>). The beneficiary‚Äôs agreement requires A‚àí. The rating must belong to the legal entity that issued the guarantee.","Match the downgrade to affected guarantees in the CRM. Pull quotes from approved banks‚Äô portals and draft the replacement request. Pause if the named issuer could be a subsidiary or branch.","Broker verifies the entity and approves outreach. The beneficiary accepts the replacement before the old guarantee is released. The issued guarantee, acceptance, and paid fee invoice close the job.","Surecomp RIVO digitizes guarantee issuance and amendments.","https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/10/Ratings-Fact-Sheet.pdf","https://rivo-support.surecomp.com/hc/en-us/articles/4409692795025-Guarantees-in-Rivo | https://rivo-support.surecomp.com/hc/en-us/articles/24245074968849-How-to-request-the-Amendment-for-Outgoing-Guarantee-in-Rivo-as-a-Corporate","Fictional business and synthetic amounts. The scenario assumes authorized Terminal access, applicable data usage rights, and access to the listed destination systems. Some BFIX and FBAK uses require additional licensing, and BVAL requires applicable access."
4,1,"Cross-system business workflow","Clearsill Bond Desk","$300 commission on a settled estate bond sale","An estate submits a thinly traded bond. Its written mandate sets a reserve at 98% of the Terminal‚Äôs BVAL evaluated bid and requires a BVAL Score of at least 6. A bid of 94.00 with a score of 7 sets a 92.12 reserve. A dealer quote supplies neither BVAL input.","Compare firm bids from two dealer portals on a net clean-price basis. Stage the best bid at 93.00. Pause on a low BVAL Score, expired bid, or inconsistent treatment of accrued interest.","Broker and executor approve the bid. Match the trade confirmation to settled custody cash and the $300 commission posting.","ICE Bonds Portfolio Auction automates bond auctions and execution.","https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/10/750114_Navigate-every-market.pdf | https://professional.bloomberg.com/products/data/enterprise-catalog/pricing/evaluated-pricing/","https://www.ice.com/fixed-income-data-services/fixed-income/ice-bonds/portfolio-auction","Fictional business and synthetic amounts. The scenario assumes authorized Terminal access, applicable data usage rights, and access to the listed destination systems. Some BFIX and FBAK uses require additional licensing, and BVAL requires applicable access."
5,1,"Cross-system business workflow","Lantern Film Receipts","20% of collected royalty shortfalls","A monthly distributor statement converts ‚Ç¨80,000 into $87,200. The contract specifies the 16:00 London Bloomberg FX fixing for that date. BFIX <GO> shows $1.1000 per euro, so the expected payout is $88,000. A live FX quote addresses a different pricing question.","Reconcile the payout in the royalty workbook and draft an $800 dispute in the distributor portal. Pause if the statement combines settlement dates or omits deductions.","Rights manager approves the claim. Match the accepted adjustment to the $800 bank receipt, then invoice the $160 success fee and track payment.","WALDHORN.AI audits royalty statements against contracts and drafts recovery letters.","https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/27/BFIX-Methodology.pdf","https://waldhorn.ai/platform/royalty-audits","Fictional business and synthetic amounts. The scenario assumes authorized Terminal access, applicable data usage rights, and access to the listed destination systems. Some BFIX and FBAK uses require additional licensing, and BVAL requires applicable access."
6,1,"Cross-system business workflow","Juniper Reset Audit","A fee when a borrower recovers excess interest","A quarterly coupon notice arrives for a legacy note that names Bloomberg‚Äôs three-month USD LIBOR fallback. FBAK <GO> shows an all-in rate of 4.62161% for the original fixing date. The servicer used 4.88322% before the note margin. Overnight SOFR alone cannot reproduce the tenor-specific fallback.","Recalculate the coupon from the signed note and draft a $10,464.40 dispute in the servicer portal on $16 million for 90/360. Pause if an amendment changes the fallback or fixing date.","Treasury approves the claim after checking the signed terms. A corrected notice and the $10,464.40 cash credit verify recovery and trigger the success-fee invoice.","Loan IQ calculates interest within the lender‚Äôs servicing workflow.","https://assets.bbhub.io/professional/sites/27/Fallbacks_FAQ_V14.1_Apr-2025.pdf | https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/10/IBOR-Fallbacks-Technical-Note.pdf","https://www.finbridge.de/trends/2020/7/20/implementing-the-ibor-transition-in-and-around-loaniq","Fictional business and synthetic amounts. The scenario assumes authorized Terminal access, applicable data usage rights, and access to the listed destination systems. Some BFIX and FBAK uses require additional licensing, and BVAL requires applicable access."
7,1,"Cross-system business workflow","Sable Mandate Audit","A success fee on reversed performance charges","A quarter-end administrator invoice uses the 1.30% unhedged Bloomberg Global Aggregate return. The signed mandate names the USD-hedged total-return series, which shows 2.00% in the Terminal‚Äôs Index Browser (IN <GO>). The account returned 1.80%, so its agreed excess-return fee is zero.","Compare the signed benchmark schedule with the administrator‚Äôs workbook. Draft a $2,000 reversal request. Pause if a side letter changes the benchmark or its effective date.","Controller approves the request. Match the amended fee statement to the $2,000 custodian credit before invoicing Sable‚Äôs fee.","Fund Recs automates performance reconciliation across administrators and internal models.","https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/10/Bloomberg-Index-Publications-Fixed-Income-Index-Methodology.pdf | https://assets.bbhub.io/professional/sites/10/775677865_Chinese_Bonds_SFCT_DIG.pdf | https://www.ssga.com/library-content/products/fund-docs/etfs/emea/supplements/fund-sup-02-spdr-bloomberg-global-aggregate-bond-en.pdf","https://www.fundrecs.com/share-class-performance-reconciliation","Fictional business and synthetic amounts. The scenario assumes authorized Terminal access, applicable data usage rights, and access to the listed destination systems. Some BFIX and FBAK uses require additional licensing, and BVAL requires applicable access."
8,1,"Cross-system business workflow","Quay Distribution Claims","A fee on dividends recovered after custody transfers","A weekly review finds a missing payment on a transferred position. The Terminal‚Äôs Corporate Actions Calendar and Dividend History (CACT <GO> and DVD <GO>) identify a $0.80 special cash dividend for the exact security. The event amount and payment date identify the cash entry to trace.","Reconcile 6,000 entitled shares against cash journals in the former and current custodian portals. Draft a $4,800 inquiry. Pause if the old account‚Äôs ledger is unavailable or another entry could represent the same payment.","Adviser confirms entitlement and approves the claim. Match the former custodian‚Äôs resolution to the $4,800 credit at the receiving custodian, then bill the recovery fee.","DTCC ClaimConnect matches and settles bilateral claims between participating institutions.","https://assets.bbhub.io/professional/sites/10/Bloomberg-Global-Equity-Indices-Non-Market-Cap-Corporate-Action-Methodology_May2023.pdf | https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/10/Dividends-Forecast-Fact-Sheet.pdf","https://www.dtcc.com/products-and-services/asset-services/corporate-actions-processing/claimconnect","Fictional business and synthetic amounts. The scenario assumes authorized Terminal access, applicable data usage rights, and access to the listed destination systems. Some BFIX and FBAK uses require additional licensing, and BVAL requires applicable access."
9,2,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Earnings beat with raised guidance","","Before earnings, save the consensus from EE <GO>. Afterward, check the release in CN <GO>. The company reports adjusted EPS of $1.08 versus $1.00 expected and guides to a full-year midpoint of $4.76 versus $4.50 consensus.","Approve a paper long if both comparisons clear your rule. Pause if the fiscal periods or accounting definitions differ.","Use HP <GO> for the entry and exit. A move from $52 to $54 gives +$2 per share before costs.","Koyfin Actuals & Consensus displays reported and estimated financial figures.","https://assets.bbhub.io/professional/sites/10/RMB-Equity-Solutions.pdf | https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/10/Getting-Started-Guide-for-Students-English.pdf","https://www.koyfin.com/help/actuals-consensus/","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
10,2,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Dividend-driven false breakdown","","A stock closes at $48.90, down from $50.00. DVD <GO> shows a $1.20 cash dividend. Check the same dates in TRA <GO> for dividend-adjusted total return.","The raw price fell 2.2%, while the price-plus-cash return is +0.2%. Reject a short signal based on the apparent price breakdown. Pause if another corporate action affects the comparison.","Log Pass with the two closes, the dividend, and the adjusted return.","TradingView provides dividend-adjusted price charts.","https://guides.library.upenn.edu/bloomberg/equities | https://www.sec.gov/divisions/corpfin/cf-noaction/14a-8/2016/jamesjensen022316-14a8.pdf","https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000590597-how-to-adjust-data-for-dividends/","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
11,2,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Buy the cheaper ETF exposure","","Compare two ETFs tracking the same index with the same currency hedge policy. NAV <GO> shows closing premiums of 0.60% and 0.05%.","Check that the NAV and price observations use comparable valuation times. If both still qualify, select the lower-premium fund for the paper allocation.","Record the 55 bp premium difference. Compare subsequent total returns for both funds to see how the choice performed.","ETF Action Data Explorer displays end-of-day premium and discount histories.","https://professional.content.cirrus.bloomberg.com/professional2023/insights/webinar/etf-go-enhancements/ | https://www.blackrock.com/gls-download/literature/investor-guide/etf-guide-for-institutional-investors.pdf","https://www.etfaction.com/pdf/terminal_user_guide.pdf","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
12,2,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Payroll surprise with a revision check","","ECO <GO> shows +170k jobs versus +190k expected, with the prior month revised from +180k to +165k. Use WB <GO> to check whether the two-year Treasury yield moved lower.","Paper-test a Treasury long when the release, revision, and yield move agree. Pause if the revision or market reaction points the other way.","Mark the same note at entry and exit. A move from 99-12 to 99-18 is a clean-price gain of 6/32 per $100 face before interest and costs.","Trading Economics Economic Calendar provides actuals, consensus and prior-period revisions.","https://data.bloomberglp.com/bat/sites/3/2016/09/LUISS-Bloomberg-Primer.pdf | https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/10/LUISS_2018Primer.pdf | https://www.cmegroup.com/education/courses/introduction-to-treasuries/calculating-us-treasury-pricing","https://tradingeconomics.com/calendar | https://docs.tradingeconomics.com/economic_calendar/schema/","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
13,2,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Crude-oil calendar spread","","Use CT <GO> to select two fixed delivery months. Their same-day settlements are $71.20 and $69.90, a $1.30 near-minus-far spread.","If the spread crosses your preset threshold, paper-test selling the near month and buying the far month. Pause if either settlement is missing or the near contract is too close to expiry.","Recheck both original contracts at exit. A spread that narrows to $0.90 gives +$0.40 per barrel before costs.","TradingView Spread Charts plots a price difference using specified contract symbols.","https://assets.bbhub.io/professional/sites/10/Proprietary-Commodity-Data-on-Bloomberg-Brochure.pdf | https://www.ice.com/publicdocs/data/ICE_on_Bloomberg.pdf","https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502298-spread-charts-explained/","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
14,2,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Callable-bond yield filter","","In YAS <GO>, compare bonds at their recorded prices. Bond A shows 5.80% to maturity and 4.40% to worst. Bond B shows 5.12% to worst.","With a 5.00% yield-to-worst floor, drop A. Keep B for review if its credit exposure and call terms fit. Pause on incomplete call terms or a stale price.","Log the price and call scenario behind the decision. If B enters the paper book, measure its price change and interest separately from the initial modeled yield.","Interactive Brokers Bond Scanner filters bonds by yield-to-worst range.","https://professional.content.cirrus.bloomberg.com/professional2023/insights/markets/bloomberg-pro-tips-analyze-and-price-bonds-on-the-go-with-yas-mobile/ | https://www.ohioapt.org/wp-content/uploads/2012/02/9A-Yacobozzi-Principles-of-Investment-Accounting.pdf","https://www.interactivebrokers.com/support/faq/content/109012775","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
15,2,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Earnings straddle break-even","","Check the event date in EVTS <GO>. In OMON <GO>, find a $100-strike call and put with the same expiry after earnings. Their combined paper purchase price is $6 per share.","Compare the trade thesis with the $94 and $106 expiry break-evens. Pause if the earnings date is uncertain or either option quote is stale.","At expiry, $108 gives +$2 per share and $103 gives ‚àí$3 per share before costs.","OptionStrat models straddle break-evens and P&L at different prices and dates.","https://assets.bbhub.io/professional/sites/10/Bloomberg_SeeAllSides.pdf | https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/4/BLPAPI-Core-User-Guide.pdf | https://www.optionseducation.org/strategies/all-strategies/long-straddle","https://optionstrat.com/tutorials/options-builder | https://optionstrat.com/build/straddle","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
16,2,"Terminal-only paper workflow","FX forward hurdle","","In FRD <GO>, check the outright EUR/USD forward for the intended value date. Spot is 1.1000, while the three-month forward is 1.1050. Use 1.1050 as the pre-cost hurdle for a paper long EUR forward.","Approve the paper test if the thesis clears the forward hurdle by your required margin. Pause if the value date or quote direction is ambiguous.","On the value date, compare against spot. 1.1120 gives +$700 on ‚Ç¨100,000 before costs.","LSEG Workspace FX Forward Curves provides forward outrights by tenor.","https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/4/BLPAPI-Core-User-Guide.pdf | https://www.iimb.ac.in/ccmrm/file/Getting-Started-Bloomberg-Basics.pdf","https://www.lseg.com/en/data-analytics/products/workspace/sales-traders/workspace-fx-trading","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
17,3,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Cash-and-stock merger spread","","Find a pending deal in MA <GO> and confirm its terms in CN <GO>. $20 cash plus 0.5 acquirer shares worth $60 each implies $50 of consideration for a target trading at $48.80.","Model buying 100 target shares and shorting 50 acquirer shares. Pause if the exchange ratio floats or the terms change.","Confirm the closing terms. Closing as signed gives +$120 gross. If the deal breaks, mark both legs using HP <GO>.","InsideArbitrage Merger Arbitrage Tracker calculates spreads for cash-and-stock deals.","https://assets.bbhub.io/professional/sites/10/RMB-Equity-Solutions.pdf | https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/10/Getting-Started-Guide-for-Students-English.pdf","https://www.insidearbitrage.com/merger-arbitrage/?dealType=Cash+Plus+Stock","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
18,3,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Buyback that actually shrinks share count","","Read repurchase cash outflow in FA <GO> and verify period-end shares in CF <GO>. The company spent $200 million repurchasing stock, while shares outstanding went from 100 million to 101 million.","Require a net decline in shares for this buyback signal. Pause if a split or mismatched reporting periods distort the comparison.","Record Pass on the buyback signal. The filings show 1% net share-count growth.","Koyfin Financial Analysis shows historical financial statements and supports custom templates for comparing line items.","https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/10/189913_CDS_REF_Fundamentals_SFCT_DIG.pdf | https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/10/2018_Bloomberg_GEI_Overview.pdf","https://www.koyfin.com/features/financial-analysis/","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
19,3,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Bond repricing after a completed refinance","","DDIS <GO> shows $650 million due within 12 months. Company news confirms $500 million of those maturities was retired. Check that the maturity schedule reflects the retirement.","Paper-test the remaining bond once the schedule shows $150 million due. Pause if repayment is pending or the new debt changes the bond‚Äôs priority.","Mark the same bond in HP <GO>. A clean-price move from 94 to 96 gives +$2 per $100 face.","Octus provides instrument-level debt stacks, maturities, and seniority data.","https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/10/750114_Navigate-every-market.pdf | https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/10/Getting-Started-Guide-for-Students-English.pdf","https://octus.com/products/mcp-connector/resources/","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
20,3,"Terminal-only paper workflow","DV01-matched Treasury steepener","","In YAS <GO>, reprice a two-year and ten-year note after a 1 bp yield change. The respective sensitivities are $20 and $80 per $100,000 face.","Paper long $400,000 face of the two-year and short $100,000 face of the ten-year. Both legs start at $80/bp. Pause if their pricing dates differ.","If yields rise 2 bp and 8 bp, the first-order gain is about $480. Verify it against both notes‚Äô closing prices.","CME Treasury Analytics shows cash and futures yield curves and DV01.","https://professional.content.cirrus.bloomberg.com/professional2023/insights/markets/bloomberg-pro-tips-analyze-and-price-bonds-on-the-go-with-yas-mobile/ | https://knowledgehub.ghamfin.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/Fixed-Income-Analysis.pdf","https://www.cmegroup.com/tools-information/quikstrike/treasury-analytics.html | https://www.cmegroup.com/tools-information/quikstrike/quikstrike-treasury-analytics-user-guide.html","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
21,3,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Three-leg FX quote check","","Use FXC <GO> and ALLQ <GO> to check USD ‚Üí EUR ‚Üí JPY ‚Üí USD. The relevant quotes are 1.1002 EUR/USD ask, 165.00 EUR/JPY bid, and 150.05 USD/JPY ask.","Calculate the round trip using the correct side of each quote. Pause if timestamps or quote sources are incompatible.","$100,000 comes back as $99,948.51. Record Pass and the $51.49 modeled loss before fees.","cTrader Algo exposes per-symbol bids and asks for custom quote checks.","https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/10/2017/03/BLPAPI-Core-User-Guide.pdf","https://help.ctrader.com/ctrader-algo/references/MarketData/Symbols/Symbols/GetSymbol/","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
22,3,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Put spread when downside skew is steep","","OVDV <GO> shows 31% implied volatility for the 25-delta put and 23% at the money for the same maturity. OMON <GO> shows a $100/$95 put spread at a $2 net debit.","If the downside thesis clears the $98 expiry break-even, paper-buy the higher strike and sell the lower strike. Pause if the leg quotes are stale.","At $94 at expiry, the spread pays $5 per share, for +$3 per share before costs. At or above $100, it loses the $2 debit.","ORATS scans on volatility metrics and backtests multi-leg options strategies.","https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/4/2015/03/education-brochure.pdf | https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/4/BLPAPI-Core-User-Guide.pdf | https://www.optionseducation.org/strategies/all-strategies/bear-put-spread","https://orats.com/option-scanner | https://orats.com/backtester","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
23,3,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Fed meeting versus the contract‚Äôs monthly average","","Check the meeting date in WIRP <GO> and select the exact Fed Funds futures month in CT <GO>. 15 days at 4.50% and 15 at 4.25% imply a 4.375% monthly average and 95.625 settlement.","Compare the scenario with a contract mark of 95.575. Stage a paper long if the difference clears your threshold. Pause if the effective date of the rate change is unclear.","If the contract settles at 95.625, the paper gain is 0.050 price points.","CME FedWatch converts monthly Fed Funds futures prices into meeting-level probabilities.","https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/10/LUISS_2018Primer.pdf | https://assets.bbhub.io/professional/sites/10/Proprietary-Commodity-Data-on-Bloomberg-Brochure.pdf | https://www.cmegroup.com/markets/interest-rates/stirs/30-day-federal-fund/specs","https://www.cmegroup.com/articles/2023/understanding-the-cme-group-fedwatch-tool-methodology.html","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
24,3,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Peer divergence with an earnings check","","COMP <GO> shows stock A trailing same-sector peer B by 4 percentage points over five sessions. Check EVTS <GO> for earnings before the planned exit.","If the event calendar is clear and company news leaves the thesis intact, paper long $10,000 of A and short $10,000 of B. Pause on a confirmed company-specific shock.","Mark both legs at the planned exit. A up 2% and B down 1% gives +$300 before costs.","QuantConnect LEAN has a prebuilt correlation-based pairs model for testing mean reversion.","https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/10/AdamLei-WP.pdf | https://assets.bbhub.io/professional/sites/10/Bloomberg_SeeAllSides.pdf","https://www.quantconnect.com/docs/v2/writing-algorithms/algorithm-framework/alpha/supported-models","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
25,4,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Refinery margin spread","","In CT <GO> and HP <GO>, match one delivery month and settlement date across WTI, RBOB gasoline, and ULSD. At $72/bbl, $2.15/gal, and $2.40/gal, the 3:2:1 crack spread is $21.80 per barrel of crude input.","To test a widening margin, paper-buy two gasoline contracts and one diesel contract against three crude contracts. Pause if dates, units, or settlements differ.","Reprice the original contracts. A spread of $23.80 at exit gives +$2 per barrel of crude input.","CME Crack Conversion Calculator computes the 3:2:1 spread from input prices.","https://assets.bbhub.io/professional/sites/10/Proprietary-Commodity-Data-on-Bloomberg-Brochure.pdf | https://www.cmegroup.com/articles/2024/trading-crack-spreads.html","https://www.cmegroup.com/tools-information/calc_crack.html","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
26,4,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Analyst upgrades hidden by a flat consensus","","In EEB <GO>, compare two snapshots for the same fiscal period. Headline EPS consensus stays at $2.00. Eight continuing analysts each raise estimates by $0.10, while two higher estimates drop out.","Test the revision signal using analysts present in both snapshots. Pause if the EPS basis or contributor identities cannot be matched.","Save both contributor lists. A paper entry at $41.00 and exit at $42.50 gives +$1.50 per share.","FactSet Estimates Broker Detail provides contributor-level estimates for like-for-like comparisons.","https://assets.bbhub.io/professional/sites/10/Bloomberg_SeeAllSides.pdf","https://go.factset.com/hubfs/Website_Downloads/Statistical%20Package%20Integration/Docs%203.0/estimates-ondemand.pdf","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
27,4,"Terminal-only paper workflow","ADR premium after currency conversion","","Verify in CF <GO> that one ADR represents two ordinary shares. Use overlapping price marks in GIP <GO> and the exchange rate from FXC <GO>. At ‚Ç¨25 per ordinary share and $1.10 per euro, parity is $55.00 against an ADR at $57.20.","Paper-short one ADR against two ordinary shares if the gap clears your hurdle. Pause if prices come from different trading hours or the receipt ratio changed.","If parity stays at $55.00 and the ADR falls to $55.50, the two-leg paper gain is $1.70 per ADR.","Citi‚Äôs DR Directory identifies the underlying listing and ordinary-share-to-receipt ratio.","https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/10/2018_Bloomberg_GEI_Overview.pdf | https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/10/Getting-Started-Guide-for-Students-English.pdf | https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/4/BLPAPI-Core-User-Guide.pdf | https://www.sec.gov/files/litigation/admin/2018/33-10586.pdf","https://depositaryreceipts.citi.com/adr/guides/unspresource.aspx?pageId=3&subpageid=173","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
28,4,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Days to cover doubled without new shorts","","SI <GO> shows 10 million reported shares short at both observations. Average daily volume falls from 2 million to 1 million, so days to cover rises from 5 to 10.","Pass if the trade requires evidence of new short positions. Use the same volume lookback at both report dates and pause if the share counts are affected by a split.","Log Pass, the unchanged reported short position, and the two volume averages.","ORTEX Short Interest tracks days to cover, reported positions, and daily estimates.","https://www.buyins.net/articles/gamesshortsellersplay.pdf | https://faq.library.upenn.edu/business/faq/45338","https://docs.ortex.com/docs/dataset-short-interest | https://docs.ortex.com/reference/stock_short_dtc_retrieve","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
29,4,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Daily-reset ETF holding-period test","","Confirm the 2√ó daily objective in the fund description or filing. Read two benchmark closes in HP <GO>. The benchmark rises 10% and then falls 10%.","Compound the daily leveraged returns of +20% and ‚àí20%. Pass if the planned holding period depends on getting twice the benchmark‚Äôs cumulative return.","The benchmark ends ‚àí1%. The idealized daily-reset position ends ‚àí4%, or ‚àí$400 on $10,000. If testing an actual ETF, check its own closing marks.","testfolio LETF Analysis simulates daily-reset leverage across historical price paths.","https://www.blackrock.com/gls-download/literature/investor-guide/etf-guide-for-institutional-investors.pdf | https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/10/2018_Bloomberg_GEI_Overview.pdf | https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/general-resources/news-alerts/alerts-bulletins/investor-alerts/sec","https://testfol.io/letf/","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
30,4,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Closed-end fund tender with proration","","Read the offer in CF <GO>. The fund trades at $9.20 and offers 98% of NAV. At a $10.00 NAV, accepted shares pay $9.80.","Stress-test 25% acceptance. The remaining shares must be worth $9.00 each to break even. Pass if your residual-share mark is $8.95.","The modeled position is worth $9.1625 per share, or $37.50 below entry per 1,000 shares. After the offer, compare with published acceptance and the residual close.","CEFConnect tracks fund NAV, discounts, and tender features.","https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/10/2018_Bloomberg_GEI_Overview.pdf | https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1836057/000119312524182259/d843794dex99a1i.htm","https://documents.nuveen.com/Documents/CEFConnect/Viewer.aspx?download=1&uniqueId=8b2fd832-ea21-4dfc-82b1-2f059b613c59","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
31,4,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Copper positioning unwind","","In COT <GO>, compare the same futures-only Managed Money series. Longs fall from 150,000 to 130,000 contracts while shorts stay at 60,000. Record the report‚Äôs publication time.","If price confirms the unwind under your rule, paper-short a fixed-month copper contract at the first eligible mark after publication. Pause if report categories differ.","Mark the same contract at exit. A move from $4.20 to $4.15 per pound gives +$0.05 per pound.","Barchart Disaggregated COT tracks position histories by trader category.","https://data.bloomberglp.com/promo/sites/12/208558_BCOM-June2018Outlook.pdf | https://www.cftc.gov/MarketReports/CommitmentsofTraders/ReleaseSchedule/index.htm | https://publicreporting.cftc.gov/stories/s/r4w3-av2u","https://www.barchart.com/futures/disaggregated-cot-reports","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
32,4,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Inflation compensation versus real yields","","Use ILBE <GO> and matched-tenor yields. The 10-year nominal yield rises from 4.10% to 4.30%, while the real yield rises from 1.70% to 1.75%. Inflation breakeven widens from 2.40% to 2.55%.","A widening-breakeven thesis clears this check. A trade that requires a 20 bp rise in real yields fails it. Pause if the maturities or timestamps differ.","A later breakeven of 2.67% verifies a +12 bp spread move from the paper entry. Use the two bonds‚Äô prices separately to calculate position P&L.","FRED Graph publishes breakeven series that can be charted alongside nominal and real yields.","https://assets.bbhub.io/professional/sites/10/LUISS-Bloomberg-Primer.pdf","https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/t5yie","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
33,5,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Treasury auction tail on the same issue","","Read the auction result in Bloomberg News. The high yield is 4.34% versus a 4.31% pre-auction when-issued yield for the same CUSIP. The auction tailed by 3 bp.","If the tail qualifies under your rule, approve a paper short at the first eligible mark after the result. Pause if the pre-auction quote is stale or belongs to a different issue.","Mark the same note. An entry at 99-09 and cover at 99-02 produces +7/32 per $100 face in clean-price P&L.","Helious Treasury Auction Tails tracks when-issued yields, high yields, and auction tails.","https://www.newyorkfed.org/medialibrary/media/research/staff_reports/sr1188.pdf | https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/10/Bloomberg-Index-Publications-Fixed-Income-Index-Methodology.pdf | https://www.cmegroup.com/education/courses/introduction-to-treasuries/calculating-us-treasury-pricing","https://helious.io/data/treasury-auction-tails","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
34,5,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Transferable rights subscription economics","","In CACS <GO> and CF <GO>, check transferability, expiry, and the subscription ratio. Four rights at $0.65 each plus a $12 subscription price imply $14.60 per new share. The common stock trades at $15.00.","Approve a paper subscription if the difference clears your cost hurdle. Pause if the rights are nontransferable or the assumed settlement misses the offer deadline.","Mark the new common share after the modeled exercise. At $14.90, the paper gain is $0.30 per new share.","ICE Corporate Actions tracks rights issues and other corporate action events.","https://assets.bbhub.io/professional/sites/10/Bloomberg-Global-Equity-Indices-Non-Market-Cap-Corporate-Action-Methodology_May2023.pdf | https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/10/2018_Bloomberg_GEI_Overview.pdf | https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1487610/000121390026032989/ea0277906-03_424b2.htm","https://www.ice.com/fixed-income-data-services/data-and-analytics/pricing-and-analytics/reference-data/corporate-actions","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
35,5,"Terminal-only paper workflow","ETF asset growth versus investor inflows","","Check FFLO <GO> and the fund‚Äôs NAV and share-count history. Assets rise from $1.00 billion to $1.05 billion as NAV rises from $20 to $21. Shares outstanding stay at 50 million.","Require confirmed net inflows for a flow-driven entry. Pause if the NAV and share-count dates differ or a share split affects the comparison.","The NAV change accounts for the full $50 million increase. Record Pass if the reported flow also shows no net inflow.","ETF Action Data Explorer tracks fund flows and assets under management.","https://www.blackrock.com/gls-download/literature/investor-guide/etf-guide-for-institutional-investors.pdf | https://www.linkedin.com/posts/bloomberg-professional-service_fflo-go-activity-7269461943877349377-r4UG","https://www.etfaction.com/our-data/ | https://www.etfaction.com/pdf/terminal_user_guide.pdf","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
36,5,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Continuous futures breakout at contract roll","","A generic natural-gas chart jumps from $2.70 to $2.90. Use CT <GO> to identify the two contracts and HP <GO> to check both settlements. The old contract went from $2.70 to $2.71 and the new one from $2.89 to $2.90.","Require a breakout in one actual contract. Pause if the generic chart uses a different roll or adjustment setting.","Log Pass on the $0.20 chart signal. Each fixed contract moved just $0.01 per MMBtu.","TradingView marks continuous-contract switches and offers roll back-adjustment.","https://assets.bbhub.io/professional/sites/10/Proprietary-Commodity-Data-on-Bloomberg-Brochure.pdf | https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/4/BLPAPI-Core-User-Guide.pdf","https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000689313-switching-continuous-futures-contracts/ | https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000685266-how-can-i-enable-backadjustment-for-continuous-futures/","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
37,5,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Treasury bill discount versus investment yield","","Load the exact Treasury bill and confirm its remaining maturity and quoted basis. A 91-day bill quoted at a 4.50% bank-discount rate costs $98.8625 per $100 face.","Convert to a comparable investment yield of about 4.615%. Clear a 4.60% hurdle only after confirming the settlement date and matching the yield conventions.","On $10,000 face, record a paper cost of $9,886.25 and redemption of $10,000, for +$113.75 held to maturity.","Excel TBILLPRICE and TBILLEQ calculate bill price and bond-equivalent yield.","https://professional.content.cirrus.bloomberg.com/professional2023/insights/markets/bloomberg-pro-tips-analyze-and-price-bonds-on-the-go-with-yas-mobile/ | https://treasurydirect.gov/marketable-securities/understanding-pricing/","https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/excel/functions/tbillprice-function | https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/excel/functions/tbilleq-function","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
38,5,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Bond price check at the intended trade size","","For the exact CUSIP, compare TRACE trades in TDH <GO> with dealer quotes in ALLQ <GO>. The last print is 94.00 on $25,000 face. A $500,000 trade printed at 95.80 and the $500,000 ask is 95.95.","Compare the ask at the intended size with your 95.25 limit. Pass at 95.95. Pause if quote size is missing or the latest trade and quote are stale.","Save both trade sizes and timestamps. The size-matched ask exceeds your limit by 0.70 points, so the paper order stays unfilled.","FINRA Fixed Income Data publishes TRACE trade data, including price, time, and volume.","https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/10/750114_Navigate-every-market.pdf | https://www.finra.org/sites/default/files/TRACE_Overview.pdf","https://syndication.finra.org/content/what-trace-and-how-can-it-help-me","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
39,5,"Terminal-only paper workflow","Intraday volume at a comparable session time","","Read regular-session intraday volume. At 11:00, the stock has traded 1.2 million shares versus an average of 0.6 million by 11:00 in comparable sessions. That is 2√ó normal volume for that time.","Paper-test the breakout only if price also clears your trigger. Pause if one volume reading includes premarket trades or comes from a shortened session.","Record the time and the comparison window. A paper entry at $50.20 and exit at $51.00 gives +$0.80 per share.","TradingView Relative Volume at Time compares cumulative volume at the same point in prior sessions.","https://data.bloomberglp.com/professional/sites/10/Getting-Started-Guide-for-Students-English.pdf | https://www.valdosta.edu/colleges/business/deans-office/documents/bloomberg-cheat-sheets/charts-and-technical-indicators.pdf","https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000705489-relative-volume-at-time/","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."
40,5,"Terminal-only paper workflow","VIX futures settlement versus spot VIX","","Use CT <GO> to identify the exact full-size VX futures contract. The future is 19.50 and spot VIX is 16.00. At expiry, VX settles to the Special Opening Quotation.","Pass if the short thesis depends on receiving the spot VIX as settlement. If paper-testing a short, record the specific expiry and settlement value to use.","If the Special Opening Quotation is 20.30, a paper short at 19.50 loses $800 per full-size contract at $1,000 per point.","Cboe Futures Settlement Prices publishes VX settlement values by contract.","https://assets.bbhub.io/professional/sites/10/Proprietary-Commodity-Data-on-Bloomberg-Brochure.pdf | https://www.cboe.com/tradable-products/vix/vix-futures/specifications | https://www.cboe.com/tradable_products/vix/vix_futures/specifications","https://www.cboe.com/markets/us/futures/market-statistics/settlement/futures/daily","Synthetic Terminal-only paper example before costs. Use comparable, available closing or delayed marks. Record the decision and later marks in NOTE <GO>. Live fills require enabled trading access."

endstream 
endobj
